// `URL.createObjectURL` takes a `MediaSource` in a window and a `Blob`
// everywhere else. `MediaSource` is the Media Source Extensions object, which
// only a window has.
//
// A browser program loses the `MediaSource` overload, which is what this form
// costs. `@env("window")` on the overload expresses it exactly, and the reason
// to keep the overlay is load time rather than the annotation: a load reads the
// transitive closure of a program's imports, so one reference from `web:url`
// puts the whole DOM in the closure of everything that touches a URL,
// `web:fetch` included. BenchmarkStdlibClosureLoad measures 45ms to 268ms warm
// and 912ms to 4.4s cold for a program importing `web:fetch` alone.
//
// Paying that for one overload is the wrong trade. #1613 has the detail.
export declare class URL {
    static createObjectURL(obj: file.Blob) -> string,
}
